node_modules
dist
.env.local
.DS_Store
.pw/storageState.json

# npm pack output — the tarball belongs in spattoo-web/vendor/, never in this repo.
# `git add -A` after a release sweeps it up otherwise (it did, in 0.1.161).
*.tgz

# Claude Code scratch. `worktrees/` holds real git worktrees checked out INSIDE the repo,
# so an untracked directory appears the moment one exists — and `npm run release` refuses
# to build from a dirty tree, which is how this was found. `settings.local.json` is per
# machine by definition.
#
# Deliberately not the whole `.claude/` directory: a committed `.claude/settings.json` is
# how project-wide hooks and permissions get shared, and blanket-ignoring the folder would
# silently swallow it the day someone adds one.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Throwaway probe scripts — `col.tmp.mjs`, `shot.tmp.mjs`. Same reasoning as `worktrees/` above:
# this repo is one working tree shared by concurrent sessions, so somebody else's half-written
# Playwright probe appears in YOUR `git status` and `npm run release` refuses to build from a dirty
# tree. Found exactly that way, twice. Ignoring the pattern is the fix; deleting the file is not,
# because it belongs to whoever is still using it.
*.tmp.mjs
# ⚠️ AND THE DOT-PREFIXED ONES, which is the same probe under a name the pattern above does not
# catch (`dev/.measure-oo.mjs`). Third time this has blocked a release; the convention above is not
# enforced anywhere, so the ignore has to cover how people actually name a throwaway rather than how
# they were asked to. Still ignoring rather than deleting — it belongs to whoever is still using it.
dev/.*.mjs


# A reference cake photo for dev/edible-prints.html. A real one is a CUSTOMER'S, and a fixture is
# not a reason to commit one — drop any photo here to see the crop previews.
dev/photo.jpg

# Reference photographs for dev/ harnesses. Local only: they are other people's work
# (Instagram/Pinterest cakes) and have no business in our git history.
dev/refs/
